From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: guard phylink calls for the PON port

PON ports deliberately have no phylink instance (134), so port->phylink is
NULL for them.  airoha_dev_open()/airoha_dev_stop() still dereferenced it:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at 0x4c
  pc : phylink_of_phy_connect+0xc/0x108
  lr : airoha_dev_open+0x2f0/0x328
  x0 : 0000000000000000
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception

Guard both call sites.  phylink_start() already had its NULL check.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 13:41:03.992486567 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 13:41:03.996486843 +0800
@@ -1928,7 +1928,7 @@
 		 * good: ethtool printed only "Link detected: no", the PHY's
 		 * read_status was never polled and the copper never linked.
 		 */
-		if (!dev->phydev) {
+		if (port->phylink && !dev->phydev) {
 			err = phylink_of_phy_connect(port->phylink,
 						     dev->dev.of_node, 0);
 			if (err) {
@@ -2018,8 +2018,10 @@
 	}
 
 	if (airhoa_is_phy_external(port)) {
-		phylink_stop(port->phylink);
-		phylink_disconnect_phy(port->phylink);
+		if (port->phylink) {
+			phylink_stop(port->phylink);
+			phylink_disconnect_phy(port->phylink);
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
